d would probably end up facing an audit from their activities if they tried to punish Exalted through official channels.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, instead they'll do it through unofficial channels, like &quot;I've got an army of worshippers and you don't&quot; or &quot;Hey Wyld Hunt, there's a Solar over here!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T03:48:57-07:00","id":849672,"title":"","content":"Between Apollo sucking cock and Sol being a bottom, I'm sensing a theme here.<br /> <br /> I wonder if &quot;How to Come All Over Ra's Face?&quot; Jen's thread about social influences will be next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T05:14:48-07:00","id":849681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/849360-lord-apollo-can-suck-my-glorious-solar-dick-nsfw?p=849672#post849672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if &quot;How to Come All Over Ra's Face?&quot; Jen's thread about social influences will be next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be more or less awkward depending on the time of day you try it - one time he's a scarab, the next a man with a falcon's head, then after that he's a ram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T06:06:28-07:00","id":849687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/849360-lord-apollo-can-suck-my-glorious-solar-dick-nsfw#post849360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P/s: Not sure if it is appropriate to ask this, but ancient Greek people has brown skin in various degree of shade, wavy hair and green/brown eyes, right ? Since Cassandra's wiki article describe her as having brown hair but Google's images tells me that she's a white redhead so eeehh....???</div> </div> </div> </div>That fresco is from the House of Menander in Pompeii, painted roughly 2000 years ago. She has light skin because there is a very, very old (back even before Cassandra's own time) artistic convention in the Mediterranean of painting males with dark skin and females with light skin. You see this in frescos from Thera (~1600 years older than that painting and ~400 years before the Trojan War), bull-leaper paintings in Crete, and Egyptian tomb paintings, just off the top of my head. I can post links when I'm not on my phone but those are fun things to google.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-21-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T09:09:41-07:00","id":849753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/849360-lord-apollo-can-suck-my-glorious-solar-dick-nsfw#post849360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/CENTER]<br /> <br /> The law of Heaven include something like &quot;Gods shouldn't mess with Creation, it belongs to the Exalted&quot;, correct ?<br /> <br /> Sooooooo is it in the Solar's rights to punish spirit who step beyond their duties like accepting bribe, terrorize human into worshiping them or having ties with the enemies of Creation ? It's hard for me to decide since I have no idea what does the law of Heaven include, what messing with Creation mean or the exact duty of the Exalted aside from vague sentence scatters among various places<br /> <br /> I don't even know what are the proper steps to punish a guilty spirit, do I instantly daiklaive the god right in their ass or do I have to make report to the Censor and let them handle it, but what if I know that the Censor is corrupted too ?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that is one of THE most beautiful Daiklaves I have ever seen! It's got me thinking about Evocations themed around beauty, involving targets awed at the sight of the most resplendent thing they'd *ever seen in their lives* being the last thing they see as it hurtles at them...<br /> <br /> Second, Exalted's subversion of the &quot;Law of Heaven&quot; is basically that Might does in fact Make Right. The laws supporting Exalted rules only have efficacy because the Exalted were powerful enough to overthrow the Primordials, who only ruled in the first place because their great power enforced their geas on the Gods (also the basis of an Infernal charm that compels spirits to stop abusing their powers and to do their damn jobs). So, &quot;morality&quot; really has very little to do with anything, and the constant harping on &quot;righteousness&quot; is basically propaganda. Frankly, the Yozis and their supporters have a point, that as the original creators and rulers, if anyone's law is &quot;true&quot;, it's theirs, but they couldn't hold onto the universe, so fuck `em. <br /> <br /> Third, the game never went into exactly what the Laws of Heaven are, and likely never will, so this is up to the ST deciding what will make their games more interesting and dramatic. You can easily take some RL inspiration here, every culture has laws that are officially still on the books, but which no one enforces anymore because times have moved on...except for that one asshole who insists on bringing it up because it benefits his position in some way!<br /> <br /> The Mandate of Heaven gave rulership over the Earth to the Exalted. Interestingly, we're not told what it says about the lack of Exalted stewardship, or if such was ever foreseen, but the implication is that, in that event, Mortals are to rule over themselves. Spirits are absolutely forbidden to rule Mortals...which seems rather odd to me, but it works to set up the situation the game needs for its setting, so ok. <br /> <br /> In the First Age, as things were supposed to work, if Spirits got too lazy or demanding, the mortals would pray to the spirits' immediate superior, who'd chastise them. If that didn't work, the traveling Censor would eventually come by, inspect the local prayers, summon all the spirits involved and demand an accounting. If all this didn't work (or the Censor was corrupt), then eventually the prayers for relief would reach the Celestial Bureaucracy in Yu-Shan, who'd start a process that would eventually end in the dispatch of Celestial Exalts (or Terrestrials if local Celestials were all too busy) to see what the problem was, which usually resolved things.<br /> <br /> In the Second Age, it plays out much like the 2E intro comic: Spirits are abusing mortals (or vice versa!), which disrupts local affairs/nature enough for a passing Circle of Solars to take notice, who then investigate the sitch, and kick ass or use The Stare until things are working in their proper order again. Matters might be complicated by spirits who are hoping to rise up the ranks by snitching on the illicit activities of their superiors, which can also be useful...Remember, most Solars probably don't know that the Law supports them just walking in and demanding the local spirit court bows to their settlement, so an obsequious spirit telling them this can be a revelation, esp to a former mortal used to bowing before the spirits for a lifetime!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T09:15:37-07:00","id":849757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/849360-lord-apollo-can-suck-my-glorious-solar-dick-nsfw?p=849378#post849378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of mythological/religious characters are depicted as fair skinned in Western art. Jesus is the biggest example of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're going to be technical about it, mythological/religious figures tend to just get depicted according to the artist's idea of &quot;default human.&quot; See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/846100-conky-is-a-slutty-bottom-in-gem\">the last Jenthread on the subject</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:37:31-07:00","id":849788,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, the thread title reminds me of a funny exchange from the great cable series Rome, between some Roman centurions in the hold of a storm-tossed ship:<br /> <br /> Centurion 1: &quot;This storm is getting worse! Didn't the captain perform the appropriate sacrifices to Neptune?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Centurion 2: &quot;If Neptune can't keep me dryer than this, then he can <i>suck my cock</i>, hahaha!!&quot;<br /> <br /> [cue shipwreck...]<br /> <br /> I've thought about putting those words in the mouths of Realm legionnaires, only about either the Ocean Father or Daana'd...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}